#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186114835 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "461c0f55-cb85-511e-b8cb-be11f8a3c250" :knowledge-point/title "Domains of Functions With Reciprocal and Radical Components"}] :question/id #uuid "9a86e942-8852-5cce-b9be-e7a5eff46d12" :question/math-academy-id "e-12350" :question/problem "Find the domain of the vector-valued function $\\mathbf f(t) = \\left\\langle \\sqrt{t+3}, \\: t^3-t^2, \\: \\dfrac{1}{t+1}\\right\\rangle$." :question/worked-solution "To find the domain of $\\mathbf{f}$, we need the intersection of the domains of the individual components.\n\n- The domain of the 1st component $\\sqrt{t+3}$ is $[MATH: t \\in [-3,\\infty).]$\n- The domain of the 2nd component $t^3-t^2$ is $t \\in (-\\infty,\\infty)$.\n- The domain of the 3rd component $\\dfrac{1}{t+1}$ is $t \\in (-\\infty,-1)\\cup(-1,\\infty)$.\n\nThe intersection is illustrated in the diagram below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1737/Source/Images/5af0a18236943f5ed868820bafbe061b.png)\n\nTherefore, the domain of the vector-valued function $\\mathbf{f}(t)$ is $[MATH: t \\in [-3,-1)\\cup(-1,\\infty).]$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186114836 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "74a1499c-080d-5008-bcc3-492ef469d3dc" :knowledge-point/title "Domains of Functions With Exponential and Logarithmic Components"}] :question/id #uuid "726fa7f3-a110-5730-a734-1019fd77de9a" :question/math-academy-id "e-12362" :question/problem "Find the domain of the vector-valued function $\\mathbf f(t)$, given by\n$\\mathbf{f} (t) = \\ln{t} \\, \\mathbf{i} + \\frac{1}{t-2} \\, \\mathbf{j} + e^{2t} \\, \\mathbf{k}$." :question/worked-solution "To find the domain of $\\mathbf{f}$, we need the intersection of the domains of the individual components.\n\n- The domain of the 1st component $\\ln{t}$ is $t \\in (0, \\infty)$.\n- The domain of the 2nd component $\\dfrac{1}{t-2}$ is $t \\in (-\\infty,2)\\cup(2,\\infty)$.\n- The domain of the 3rd component $e^{2t}$ is $t \\in (-\\infty,\\infty)$.\n\nThe intersection is illustrated in the diagram below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1737/Source/Images/40ca4990aa765c6a975686a987f4f47c.png)\n\nTherefore, the domain of the vector-valued function $\\mathbf{f}(t)$ is $t \\in (0,2)\\cup (2,\\infty)$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186114837 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "553f7b9d-c387-59b0-a0d6-9624d012e414" :knowledge-point/title "Domains of Functions With Trigonometric Components"}] :question/id #uuid "a63854e6-412b-5308-be28-c05337aa4b9b" :question/math-academy-id "e-12455" :question/problem "The domain of the vector-valued function $\\mathbf f (t) = \\tan\\left(t+\\dfrac{\\pi}{6} \\right) \\, \\mathbf i + t^3 \\,\\mathbf j + e^t \\,\\mathbf k$ is\n$t\\in (-\\infty,\\infty), \\quad t \\neq \\bbox[5pt, border:1pt solid black]{\\phantom{AAAAA}}$.\nWhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "To find the domain of $\\mathbf{f}$, we need the intersection of the domains of the individual components.\n\n- The domain of the 1st component $\\tan\\left(t+\\dfrac{\\pi}{6} \\right)$ is $t \\in (-\\infty,\\infty)$, except for the values of $t$ for which\n$t+\\dfrac{\\pi}{6} = \\dfrac{\\pi}{2} + n\\pi \\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad t = \\dfrac{\\pi}{3} + n\\pi$,\nwhere $n$ is an integer.\n- The domain of the 2nd component $t^3$ is $t \\in (-\\infty,\\infty)$.\n- The domain of the 3rd component $e^{t}$ is $t \\in (-\\infty,\\infty)$.\n\nTherefore, the domain of the vector-valued function $\\mathbf{f}(t)$ is\n\n$$\nt\\in (-\\infty,\\infty), \\quad t \\neq \\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\dfrac{\\pi}{3} + n\\pi}\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is an integer."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115430 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "74a1499c-080d-5008-bcc3-492ef469d3dc" :knowledge-point/title "Domains of Functions With Exponential and Logarithmic Components"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "841ffaf5-a4e7-5703-9181-7b110713ef61" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s ∈ (-1, ∞)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186112024} {:answer/id #uuid "c2932588-f1b5-5a33-98e0-c51ac88e6f17" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s ∈ (- ∞, 1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186112025} {:answer/id #uuid "d06707e3-33c5-5c89-a5d0-d51f8909da77" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s ∈ (-1, 0)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186112026} {:answer/id #uuid "dc6c91e6-5936-5ee2-bdda-35f2d645d86e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s ∈ (0, 1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186112027} {:answer/id #uuid "7c919f64-4a99-5652-84f0-ea3b36aa3fad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s ∈ (-1, 1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186112028}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7c919f64-4a99-5652-84f0-ea3b36aa3fad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s ∈ (-1, 1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186112028} :answer-field/id #uuid "2f8c365d-bd9c-5da2-974f-8d544ba75c21" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186112023}] :question/id #uuid "56023ec9-5ce1-5f4b-8f47-3c4d6d6b2dd7" :question/math-academy-id "q-160789" :question/problem "Find the domain of the vector-valued function $f(s) = ⟨\\ln (1 + s), \\ln (1 - s), \\frac{1}{1 + s}⟩$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115431 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "461c0f55-cb85-511e-b8cb-be11f8a3c250" :knowledge-point/title "Domains of Functions With Reciprocal and Radical Components"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "97203691-47ee-575b-8d27-1fa58ccf6265" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t ∈ (-2, 0)∪(0, ∞)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186112030} {:answer/id #uuid "17e8504d-2fee-50eb-afd4-b9c7aa315223" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[MATH: t ∈ [2, ∞)]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186112031} {:answer/id #uuid "1ee13715